# Read by the release workflow's packager, which uploads the built zip to
# CurseForge over the API. CurseForge's own repository packaging must stay OFF:
# with both running, every tag would produce two competing files.
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1639171
## SavedVariables: PostboxDB
## OptionalDeps: EllesmereUI, EllesmereUIBlizzardSkin, ElvUI, ElvUI_WindTools

# Foundation layer. Core/Helpers.lua captures Lib\Util.lua's functions by
# reference and Core/Theme.lua binds Lib\UI\Theme.lua at load time, so the whole
# of Lib\ must load before Core\.
Lib\Store.lua
Lib\Events.lua
Lib\Util.lua
Lib\InventoryLock.lua
Lib\UI\Theme.lua
Lib\UI\Window.lua
Lib\UI\Dropdown.lua

# Postbox
Core\Locales.lua
Postbox.lua
Core\Helpers.lua
Core\Recipients.lua
# Reads ns.Recipients (R.Key / R.NormalizeRealm) and ns.Helpers, so it follows
# both; Core\SendTab.lua is its only consumer and loads later still.
Core\MailRules.lua
Core\Theme.lua
Core\MailService.lua
Core\ContactService.lua
Core\CollectTab.lua
Core\SendTab.lua
Core\MailboxUI.lua
Core\MailMemory.lua
Core\MinimapButton.lua
Core\OptionsPanel.lua
Core\RecipientManager.lua

# Skins. Skin_Modern is first-party (claims only on the plain UI when the
# style option asks for it); the host-UI files are inert unless their host is
# installed. EllesmereUI loads last and wins when both hosts are present (see
# Skin_EllesmereUI.lua).
Core\Skin_Modern.lua
Core\Skin_ElvUI.lua
Core\Skin_EllesmereUI.lua